Loop Deck: third-party licenses

Runtime dependencies: none.

The Loop Deck programs (the server, the generator and the contract checker) import only the Python
standard library (Python 3.9 or newer). The standard library comes with the Python interpreter under the
Python Software Foundation License; no part of Python is included here. The page (index.html, app.js,
app.css) bundles no third-party script, style sheet or font: it uses the system's own fonts, fetches
only from the server's own origin, and loads mermaid.min.js only when an operator supplies it (below).

Not included, optional at run time:

  mermaid 11 (MIT License). If an operator places mermaid.min.js beside index.html in the served
  directory, the page uses it to draw the Topology and Runbook diagrams. That copy is the operator's
  and keeps its own license; without it the page shows each diagram's source.

Not included, optional for the tests only:

  node. When node is on PATH, the rendered page checks in tests/test_loop_deck_spa.py run the page's
  app.js under node in a fake DOM; without it those checks skip. Running Loop Deck does not need node.
